1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,180
Trees have muscles.
树有肌肉。

2
00:00:01,180 --> 00:00:04,180
And they know when they are bent, even with their eyes closed.
而且它闭着眼，也知道自己歪了。

3
00:00:04,180 --> 00:00:04,910
Bend one over,
把它压弯，

4
00:00:04,910 --> 00:00:07,070
and it will slowly pull itself back up.
它会自己慢慢挺回来。

5
00:00:07,070 --> 00:00:08,630
French scientists just showed it,
法国科学家刚刚证明了这件事，

6
00:00:08,630 --> 00:00:10,730
using a machine that never stops spinning.
用的是一台会转的机器。

7
00:00:10,730 --> 00:00:13,100
Their paper just came out in New Phytologist.
论文刚登在《新植物学家》上。

8
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:14,960
Yes, that is a real journal name.
对，这本期刊真叫这个名字。

9
00:00:14,960 --> 00:00:16,170
Start with an experiment:
先来个实验：

10
00:00:16,170 --> 00:00:18,040
lay a young poplar tree on its side.
把一棵小杨树放倒。

11
00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:19,020
In about ten days,
大约十天，

12
00:00:19,020 --> 00:00:21,290
its stem curves back up toward the sky.
它的茎就弯着朝上长回来。

13
00:00:21,290 --> 00:00:22,170
No surprise there.
这不奇怪，

14
00:00:22,170 --> 00:00:24,190
Trees feel gravity and chase the light.
树能感觉重力，也追着光走。

15
00:00:24,190 --> 00:00:25,260
Today's brain teaser:
今天的烧脑问题：

16
00:00:25,260 --> 00:00:28,510
what if there is no gravity direction and no light direction?
要是没有重力方向，也没有光的方向呢？

17
00:00:28,510 --> 00:00:29,660
Does the tree still know
树还知道

18
00:00:29,660 --> 00:00:30,550
that it is bent?
自己是弯的吗？

19
00:00:30,550 --> 00:00:32,460
Think about it: a tree has no eyes,
想想看：树没有眼睛，

20
00:00:32,460 --> 00:00:34,220
no brain, no nerves like ours.
也没有我们那样的大脑和神经。

21
00:00:34,220 --> 00:00:35,550
The team built a machine:
研究团队造了一台机器：

22
00:00:35,550 --> 00:00:37,320
a platform that slowly rotates.
一个慢慢转的平台。

23
00:00:37,320 --> 00:00:38,370
The tree lies on it
树横躺在上面，

24
00:00:38,370 --> 00:00:40,260
and turns, and turns, and turns.
一直转，一直转。

25
00:00:40,260 --> 00:00:42,330
So gravity never points one steady way.
这样重力就没有固定的方向，

26
00:00:42,330 --> 00:00:44,250
For the tree, down keeps changing.
从树的角度看，“下面”一直在变。

27
00:00:44,250 --> 00:00:46,110
The whole thing sits inside a sphere
整个装置罩在一个球里，

28
00:00:46,110 --> 00:00:47,670
lit equally from every side.
四面八方的光一样亮。

29
00:00:47,670 --> 00:00:48,490
No up, no down,
没有上，没有下，

30
00:00:48,490 --> 00:00:49,420
no bright side.
也没有哪边更亮。

31
00:00:49,420 --> 00:00:51,300
Basically, a tree on a rotisserie,
说白了：一棵放在烤肉架上转的树，

32
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:52,970
inside a giant glowing ball.
还装在一个发光的大球里。

33
00:00:52,970 --> 00:00:54,710
The result: over the next few weeks,
结果：接下来几周，

34
00:00:54,710 --> 00:00:56,720
the bent stems slowly straightened out.
弯的茎慢慢变直了。

35
00:00:56,720 --> 00:00:57,630
Almost as straight
几乎直得像

36
00:00:57,630 --> 00:00:59,160
as if nothing ever happened.
什么都没发生过。

37
00:00:59,160 --> 00:01:00,180
And it was not luck.
而且不是碰巧。

38
00:01:00,180 --> 00:01:02,230
Something inside the tree was pulling.
树的身体里有东西在拉。

39
00:01:02,230 --> 00:01:04,450
Twist one: the tree was not using gravity.
反转一：树靠的不是重力，

40
00:01:04,450 --> 00:01:06,100
It was sensing its own shape.
是对自己形状的感觉。

41
00:01:06,100 --> 00:01:07,850
That sense is called proprioception.
这叫本体感觉。

42
00:01:07,850 --> 00:01:10,490
It is how you touch your nose with your eyes closed.
你闭上眼也能摸到鼻子，靠的就是它。

43
00:01:10,490 --> 00:01:12,940
Back in 2012, the same institute showed
二零一二年，同一家研究所就证明了：

44
00:01:12,940 --> 00:01:15,070
that plants have proprioception.
植物有本体感觉。

45
00:01:15,070 --> 00:01:16,140
Robots have it too:
机器人也有：

46
00:01:16,140 --> 00:01:19,150
a sensor in every joint reports how far it is bent.
每个关节里有个传感器，报告自己弯了多少。

47
00:01:19,150 --> 00:01:21,060
So how does a tree pull itself straight?
那树用什么把自己掰直？

48
00:01:21,060 --> 00:01:22,520
With a special kind of wood.
答案是一种特别的木头。

49
00:01:22,520 --> 00:01:23,870
It is called tension wood,
它叫应拉木，

50
00:01:23,870 --> 00:01:26,060
and it grows along one side of the stem.
长在弯的那一边。

51
00:01:26,060 --> 00:01:27,820
Tension wood shrinks and pulls,
应拉木会收缩、往回拉，

52
00:01:27,820 --> 00:01:29,020
just like a muscle.
就像一块肌肉。

53
00:01:29,020 --> 00:01:30,600
Not fast, like your muscles.
不像你的肌肉那么快，

54
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:32,470
It builds up as new wood grows.
它是随着新木头一点点长出来的。

55
00:01:32,470 --> 00:01:33,990
While the tree curves back up,
树弯着朝上长回来的时候，

56
00:01:33,990 --> 00:01:36,200
the tension wood forms on the upper side.
应拉木在上面那一侧。

57
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:37,560
Twist two, the clever one:
反转二，最妙：

58
00:01:37,560 --> 00:01:40,670
once the machine starts, that upper muscle stops growing.
机器一转，上面这块肌肉不长了。

59
00:01:40,670 --> 00:01:42,040
And identical tension wood
一模一样的应拉木，

60
00:01:42,040 --> 00:01:44,060
starts growing on the opposite side.
长到了对面去。

61
00:01:44,060 --> 00:01:45,170
It is like your arm:
就像你的手臂：

62
00:01:45,170 --> 00:01:47,390
biceps bend it, triceps straighten it.
二头肌把它弯起来，三头肌把它伸直。

63
00:01:47,390 --> 00:01:48,090
The two pulls
两边的力

64
00:01:48,090 --> 00:01:49,230
slowly balance out.
慢慢扯平。

65
00:01:49,230 --> 00:01:50,310
And that is how the tree
树就这样

66
00:01:50,310 --> 00:01:51,420
pulls itself straight.
把自己掰直了。

67
00:01:51,420 --> 00:01:53,580
Picture a flagpole with a rope on each side:
想象一根旗杆，两边各拴一根绳：

68
00:01:53,580 --> 00:01:55,720
pull both just right, and it stands tall.
拉得刚好，它就站得笔直。

69
00:01:55,720 --> 00:01:58,830
The research director calls it a genuine sensorimotor loop
研究主任说，这是树木木头里

70
00:01:58,830 --> 00:02:00,450
in the woody parts of trees.
一个真正的感觉加运动的回路。

71
00:02:00,450 --> 00:02:02,210
Feel the bend, grow the muscle,
感觉到弯，就长肌肉，

72
00:02:02,210 --> 00:02:03,750
feel again, adjust again.
再感觉，再调整。

73
00:02:03,750 --> 00:02:05,810
That is the same idea a robot uses
这跟机器人站稳的办法

74
00:02:05,810 --> 00:02:07,150
to keep its balance.
是同一个思路。

75
00:02:07,150 --> 00:02:09,940
Except a robot adjusts hundreds of times a second.
只不过机器人一秒钟调几百次，

76
00:02:09,940 --> 00:02:11,110
A tree takes weeks.
树要调好几个星期。

77
00:02:11,110 --> 00:02:11,690
Same loop.
同一个回路，

78
00:02:11,690 --> 00:02:13,140
Wildly different speed.
速度天差地别。

79
00:02:13,140 --> 00:02:14,810
Twist three, the useful one:
反转三，跟你有关：

80
00:02:14,810 --> 00:02:15,710
this matters.
有用。

81
00:02:15,710 --> 00:02:17,200
After storms and landslides,
暴风雨、山体滑坡之后，

82
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:19,390
trees need this trick to stand back up.
树要靠这招重新站直。

83
00:02:19,390 --> 00:02:21,670
Breeding trees with a stronger sense of shape
挑本体感觉更强的品种，

84
00:02:21,670 --> 00:02:23,570
might give straighter, better wood.
也许能长出更直、更好的木材。

85
00:02:23,570 --> 00:02:24,820
Messy internal tension
内部拉力太乱，

86
00:02:24,820 --> 00:02:26,300
can make the wood worse.
木头质量会变差。

87
00:02:26,300 --> 00:02:27,570
The researchers even hope
研究者还想到：

88
00:02:27,570 --> 00:02:29,630
it could keep wheat from falling over.
也许能让麦子少倒伏。

89
00:02:29,630 --> 00:02:30,890
Farmers call it lodging,
农民管这叫倒伏，

90
00:02:30,890 --> 00:02:32,380
and it costs real harvest.
会实打实地减产。

91
00:02:32,380 --> 00:02:34,640
Fine print: these were young poplars in a lab.
友情提示：这是小杨树在实验室里的实验，

92
00:02:34,640 --> 00:02:36,820
Big trees in the wild still need checking.
大树在野外怎么样，还要再看。

93
00:02:36,820 --> 00:02:38,400
And muscle is a metaphor.
“肌肉”是比喻，

94
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:40,160
Wood is not actual muscle.
木头不是真的肌肉。

95
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:42,370
The paper says it is controlled cell by cell.
论文说这是一个细胞一个细胞控制的，

96
00:02:42,370 --> 00:02:44,400
The details are still being worked out.
细节还在研究。

97
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:47,170
So, does a tree know it is bent with its eyes closed?
所以，树闭着眼知道自己歪了吗？

98
00:02:47,170 --> 00:02:48,640
Yes. Then it hits the gym.
知道，然后它去健身。

99
00:02:48,640 --> 00:02:50,210
The slowest gym in the world.
世界上最慢的健身房，

100
00:02:50,210 --> 00:02:52,280
One workout takes several weeks.
一次训练，好几个星期。

